# `show(sheet.title, sheet.rows)` is handed the sheet, through two projections: inside `show`, `title` and `rows` hold
# it, so the loop goes over the sheet, and `print(title, ..)` reads it. Where the plan cannot pair what a call hands with
# the parameters it fills (#157), a parameter still holds no value from beyond the route: it is a value of the body
# whose parameter it is, made by no step the plan follows, in that body's frame (#159). Closed, `show` takes no `Row`
# from beyond.

route sheets.run
step run/show
step run/show/for row in rows

line entry > run call
line Sheet·sheet > run value
line Sheet·sheet > run/show value                                      # `print(title, ..)`, the title of the sheet
known #157 line Sheet·sheet > run/show/for row in rows value          # `rows` holds `sheet.rows`
line run/show/for row in rows > Row·row@run/show/for row in rows value
known #101 line Row·row@run/show/for row in rows > run/show value     # `row.text`
line run/show > Screen own
known #157 extra line Row·rows@run/show/~rows > run/show/for row in rows value   # the parameter, bound by no value the call hands
known #157 extra home Row·rows@run/show/~rows run/show

home Sheet·sheet run
home Row·row@run/show/for row in rows run/show

side entry left
side Screen right
